--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,17 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Tool input is validated against a tool's declared `inputSchema` before its executor runs. A call the
+  schema rejects no longer reaches the executor and no longer ends the conversation as an error:
+  `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property path and the
+  constraint that failed — never a property value — and the orchestrator feeds that text back to the
+  model as a `tool_result`, so it can correct the call within the existing tool-round budget. Schemas
+  compile once at registration, so a tool with an uncompilable `inputSchema` fails at startup with an
+  error naming the tool. Executors that hand-validated their own input now receive only what the schema
+  accepts; extra properties still pass through untouched.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17
 
 ### Changed
