-- Cast input fields from `unknown` to their expected types
-- Handle missing or unknown input gracefully (return a reasonable default or error message)
+- Treat `input` as schema-valid: the registry has already checked it against `inputSchema`, so required fields are present with their declared types -- no defensive casting or missing-input handling needed
+- Expect unknown keys anyway: the schema does not exclude extra properties, so an undeclared key can arrive -- ignore what you did not declare
